WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.367
-Hey, welcome back.
Welcome back.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:03.868
-Thank you, buddy.
I'm happy to be back.

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.968
Oh, my God, please. I'm happy.
Thank you for doing the show.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.434
I have thousands of things
I want to talk to you about.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:10.133
But first, I'm happy
that we're friends.

00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:13.601
We know each other a little bit,
and I know that --

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.801
And I just don't want to call
you really out on the show.

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:18.534
But you've been collecting
these things,

00:00:18.534 --> 00:00:19.934
and I think we should
talk about them

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:22.000
'cause it makes me laugh.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.334
So I started collecting VHSs

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:28.434
that were sealed in the box
like three years ago

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:32.400
'cause I was really high
one night and I thought --

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.734
I thought, 'cause, like,
listen to this, guys.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:39.033
So in 2026, it'll be 20 years

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.133
since the last VHS
was made, right?

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.501
So 20 years goes by,

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.133
that's enough time
for people to be like,

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.367
"Oh, that was cool. Remember?"

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.567
Like vinyl.
-Yes.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.167
-So I bought all the sealed ones
that exist,

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.868
like 3,000 to 5,000 tapes.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:54.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:55.767
You guys sound like my mom.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.167
-No, no.
-No one believes in me.

00:00:58.167 --> 00:01:00.300
No one believes in me.
-Look at this. This is --

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.133
-Oh, yeah, that's just --
yeah, that's just --

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.100
-Here's some of the packages
that arrived at your house.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:08.634
-That's at my --
That's at my assistant's house.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:12.234
And his girlfriend
is very mad at him.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:15.100
-You have that --
-I have about 3,000 to 5,000.

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.133
But hear me out.
Hear me out.

00:01:16.133 --> 00:01:19.834
So as of a month ago,

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:24.934
sealed VHSs are now going
for like 20 to 30 grand a pop.

00:01:24.934 --> 00:01:26.767
Ooh!

00:01:26.767 --> 00:01:27.934
-That's not --

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:31.434
-"Rocky" just sold
for like $27,000.

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:32.434
-What?
-Yes.

00:01:32.434 --> 00:01:35.234
-You're serious?
-Yeah. It's my GameStop.

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:39.367
Like, this is my --
Like, dude, I own all of them.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:42.167
-This is your Game--
-Dude, no one believed in me.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.400
-Wow!

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.767
We believe in you now, Pete.
We believe in you.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.701
-It's gonna happen, you guys.
-This is great.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:52.400
It's a disaster.
-It's a -- Dude.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.968
If it doesn't work, dude, I'm
gonna be on the road forever.

00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:56.901
-It's a disaster, yeah.

00:01:56.901 --> 00:01:59.501
Last time you were here, I was
so excited to have you here.

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:01.601
You were excited. You were about
to host "Saturday Night Live."

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:02.767
-Yeah.
-It was like, wow.

00:02:02.767 --> 00:02:04.400
And then the writers'
strike happened.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.968
-Of course. Yeah.
-And you weren't able to host.

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.267
-No.
-No.

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.234
And it was that week, actually.
-It was that week.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:13.467
It's funny, any time
I have something

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:16.033
that I work really hard on
that I'm, like, really proud of,

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:19.534
either, like,
a national pandemic happens

00:02:19.534 --> 00:02:22.267
and they're like,
"No premiere for you."

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.801
-Yeah.
-And then, yeah,

00:02:23.801 --> 00:02:25.334
and then this writers'
strike happened.

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.501
So, yeah, I still don't think --
It might not happen.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.567
-No, no, no. It's going to --
It's going to happen.

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:30.834
I'm excited about this.

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:32.033
How did you find out
that you were going to host?

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:34.300
-Oh, I got a classic Lorne text.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:37.033
He was like,
"There's a rumor going around

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.801
that you're the host
for the premiere."

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:42.200
And he goes, "I guess it's true,
because I started it."

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.767
[ Laughter ]
-That's pretty good.

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.601
-I mean, he's --
-He's the best.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.334
-He's the best with the liners.
-He's the best with the liners.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.834
And I know your mom is one
of your biggest supporters,

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:51.801
and I've seen her on the show.

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:52.934
Is she excited?
Is she coming?

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:54.434
-She's very excited.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.067
She actually has been
on the show

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.934
almost as many times as I have.

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:00.300
Like, she's always ready
to go up.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.534
-That's actually really funny.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.601
-And I'm really excited
just because,

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:07.901
like, I'm trying to find my mom,
like, someone to date.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.834
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:12.467
She hasn't been with anybody
in like 23 years,

00:03:12.467 --> 00:03:14.434
so, like, yeah.
-This is a big deal.

00:03:14.434 --> 00:03:16.467
-Yeah, and she's a good catch.
-She is.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.767
-Yeah.
-She's fantastic.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.834
-Yeah, and it's, like, you know,
brand-new down there.

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:22.067
So, if...

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:24.067
[ Rim shot ]

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:26.167
If anybody --

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.267
No, I've been trying to --
Do you know anyone?

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.234
Like, I've been trying
to find someone nice,

00:03:30.234 --> 00:03:31.834
you know, for my mom, so...

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.300
-Yeah, we have --

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.701
Do you have any
single people out there?

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.467
-Yeah. Well, no, not --
[ Audience cheering ]

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.534
No, not you guys.
-No, no, no.

00:03:38.534 --> 00:03:39.901
No.
-No, yeah, someone --

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:41.300
-Out there, someone out there.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.734
Who is she looking for?
What kind of man does she want?

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.467
-I don't know.
She's never really talked --

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.467
We're not --
We don't talk about that stuff.

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:51.434
But I really just want
someone to take care of her

00:03:51.434 --> 00:03:53.534
and get her off of my hands.

00:03:53.534 --> 00:03:54.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.834
-But she will be there, right,
and supporting you?

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:58.200
-Oh, yeah.
-You know what I read?

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.200
It made me laugh
because my parents

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.000
did kind of a similar thing,
but is this true?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:06.000
She made you take
the sanitation exam?

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:10.167
-Yes. And when I got "SNL,"
I called her and I was like,

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.601
"I'm going to be --
I got 'SNL,' Mom.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.534
Like, holy crap.
Like, wow."

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.467
And she was like,
"Well, just so you know,

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:19.934
the garbageman test is at
the end of the month in case --"

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:22.234
So she -- Until about
three years ago,

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.534
every year. she would ask me
to take the garbageman test

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.234
just as, like, a backup.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.968
-And how did you do?

00:04:27.968 --> 00:04:30.367
-I didn't take it, but she would
always try to be like --

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.734
She's like,
"It's pretty cool, Peter

00:04:31.734 --> 00:04:34.267
You get to, like, hang
outside of the, you know --"

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:35.400
-No, you get to
hang off the side.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.267
She's like,
"That'd be good for you."

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:38.801
-You'd be good at that, yeah.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:39.934
-My parents, same thing.

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.767
They go, "Jimmy,
we love your comedy career.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:43.701
You want to be a comedian.
That's so cool.

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.234
Take the postal exam."

00:04:45.234 --> 00:04:47.834
-Yeah, you get to drive
on the other side.

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.601
-I love --
You get to drive --

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:51.534
Your steering wheel's
on the other side.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.167
You wear shorts to work.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.400
I mean,
they got their own rules.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.767
-It's an Irish thing.
-It's an --

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:57.734
-They don't believe in us.
-They don't believe in us.

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.400
No. Yeah, but look --
look at you now, though.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.234
Hosting "Saturday Night Live,"
Mom.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.601
-Yeah.
-This is a big deal.

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.868
-Oh, thanks. Yeah, I'm stoked.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.868 --> 00:05:07.667
-In your 20s.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:09.567
You're turning --
You're turning 30.

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:12.133
-I'm going to be 30 in a month.
Isn't that scary?

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:13.868
-Wow. It's a milestone.
-Ohh!

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:15.067
-It's a milestone.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:16.701
-Some people were like,
"I thought you were 40."

00:05:16.701 --> 00:05:18.934
-No, no, no.
No, you're young, kid.

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:20.601
-No, it's scary.
-No.

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:22.100
-It's scary to turn 30.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.434
-It's exciting.
-Yeah. I mean, it's over.

00:05:24.434 --> 00:05:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.300
No, because it's like
when you're 30,

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.367
like, if you mess up,
like, you're just, like,

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.801
a drug addict or an adult.

00:05:30.801 --> 00:05:33.334
You know what I mean?
In your 20s, you could mess up

00:05:33.334 --> 00:05:34.601
because, like, you know,
they're like,

00:05:34.601 --> 00:05:36.400
"Oh, he's finding himself."

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.033
-But 30 means something.

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:42.367
-No, now if I mess up, it, like,
matters, you know, so...

00:05:42.367 --> 00:05:44.033
-But, no, you're not
going to mess up.

00:05:44.033 --> 00:05:45.701
-No, it'll be fine.
Yeah.

00:05:45.701 --> 00:05:47.067
-I wanted to see you

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:48.567
'cause you were out
with two of my favorites,

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:51.067
John Mulaney and Jon Stewart.
-Oh, yeah, Stew.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:52.868
-On tour with --

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.767
That's an unbelievable show.

00:05:54.767 --> 00:05:56.467
-Yeah, they're great.

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:58.200
-You're great, too.
-No, no.

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.067
It's really fun
to go on the road with them.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:01.601
And it's also fun to see --

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:04.434
You could tell immediately
who's there for who.

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:06.367
-Yeah.
-Like, you know.

00:06:06.367 --> 00:06:08.567
Like, there's, like,
very respectful people

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.133
that are, like,
there to watch comedy,

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.133
and then people that are just
like, "Show us your [bleep]"

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:15.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:17.400
-Who are Jon Stewart fans.
-Those are Jon Stewart fans.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.300
-Jon Stewart fans, of course.
Yeah, yeah, of course.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.067
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's what happens, yeah.

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:25.033
-So it's a very mixed audience.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.634
-I'm so happy that
you're hosting the show.

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:31.200
I'm excited for you,
and you more than deserve it.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.968
And Ice Spice is musical guest.
-Yeah, Ice Spice.

00:06:32.968 --> 00:06:35.000
-It's a hot show this Saturday.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.667
Pete Davidson,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:06:36.667 --> 00:06:39.200
Catch him hosting
the season premiere

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.934
of "Saturday Night Live"
this weekend

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:43.634
with musical guest Ice Spice.

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:46.033
Troye Sivan joins us
after the break.

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:47.133
Stick around, everybody.

